      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll check what's in my working directory before writing the improved test.Now I have enough context. I'll write the improved test with better variable names, a descriptive comment, and clearer organization — keeping all the same method calls and arguments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`noIgnoredProperties`, `valueWithMerge`, `valueWithoutMerge`, `emptyObjectSet`), adds a Javadoc comment explaining the test's intent, and groups assertions with inline comments clarifying what each block verifies — all while preserving the exact same method calls, arguments, and expected outcomes."
